# Linkup API Documentation

- [Introduction](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/get-started/introduction.md): The production-grade web search API for AI.
- [Quickstart](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/get-started/quickstart.md): Integrate with Linkup in 5 minutes
- [For AI agents](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/get-started/for-agents.md): Download the Linkup knowledge pack for agents: what you can build, which API to call, and how to write optimized queries and workflows.
- [Search overview](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/search/overview.md): Agentic web search with four depths and three output types: sources and snippets, sourced answers, or structured JSON.
- [Search best practices](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/search/best-practices.md): Depth selection, per-depth query patterns, source filtering, and schema design for /search.
- [Search for AI agents](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/search/for-agents.md): Self-contained /search integration prompt for coding agents (Cursor, Claude Code, etc.) and tool-using LLMs.
- [Fetch overview](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/fetch/overview.md): Real-time page content extractor. Clean, LLM-ready markdown from any public URL — HTML or PDF — with optional typed JSON from the same page.
- [Fetch best practices](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/fetch/best-practices.md): Retrieval modes, JavaScript rendering, structured JSON from a known URL, pairing /fetch with /search, and operational constraints.
- [Fetch for AI agents](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/fetch/for-agents.md): Self-contained /fetch integration prompt for coding agents and tool-using LLMs that need full page content or typed JSON from a known URL.
- [Research overview](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/research/overview.md): Research agent that navigates the web to produce sourced answers, from precise factual claims to multi-section reports.
- [Research best practices](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/research/best-practices.md): Mode and reasoning-depth selection, question phrasing, polling, and failure handling for /research.
- [Research for AI agents](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/research/for-agents.md): Self-contained /research integration prompt for coding agents and tool-using LLMs that need multi-step web research.
- [Tasks overview](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/tasks/overview.md): Asynchronous batch wrapper around /search, /fetch, and /research.
- [Tasks best practices](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/tasks/best-practices.md): When to use /tasks, batch sizing, polling strategy, error handling, and cost considerations.
- [Tasks for AI agents](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/tasks/for-agents.md): Self-contained /tasks integration prompt for coding agents that need to run Linkup searches asynchronously in batch.
- [Extract overview](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/extract/overview.md): Closed-beta agent that turns a web page into structured rows of data, delivered as a downloadable NDJSON file.
- [Extract best practices](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/extract/best-practices.md): Query phrasing, schema design, URL verification, polling, and failure handling for /extract.
- [Extract for AI agents](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/extract/for-agents.md): Self-contained /extract integration prompt for coding agents that need structured data extraction from the web (closed beta).
- [Pricing](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/platform/pricing.md): How the Linkup API pricing system works
- [Authentication](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/platform/authentication.md): Authenticate with the Linkup API
- [x402 Payment Protocol](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/platform/x402.md): Pay per request with USDC on Base. No account needed.
- [Errors](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/platform/errors.md): Linkup API errors and how to handle them
- [Rate Limits](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/platform/rate-limits.md)
- [Migrating from SerpAPI](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/migrating-from-serpapi.md): Guide for switching from SerpAPI to Linkup
- [Migrating from Tavily](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/migrating-from-tavily.md): Guide for switching from Tavily Search and Extract to Linkup Search and Fetch
- [Migrating from Exa](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/migrating-from-exa.md): Guide for switching from Exa Search, Contents, and Answer to Linkup Search and Fetch
- [Structured Output Guide](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/structured-output-guide.md): How to take advantage of Structured Outputs
- [Source Filtering](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/filtering.md): How to filter your search on sources.
- [Find LinkedIn Profiles](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/linkedin-profile.md): A practical guide to quickly locate official LinkedIn home‑page URLs for companies or people
- [Signup Radar ](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/signup-radar.md): Building a signup radar to get to know your new users
- [Company Intelligence Engine](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/company-intelligence/company-intelligence.md): Build a real-time company research system using the Linkup API.
- [Peers Finder](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/peers-finder/peers-finder.md): Learn how to find comparable companies using the Linkup API with Google Sheets
- [Company Descriptions Generator](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/company-descriptions.md): Building a tool to generate rich company descriptions using Linkup API
- [Automating Lead Qualification](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/company-data-enrichment.md): Learn how to automatically research and score your leads using Linkup AI to prioritize high-value prospects
- [Meeting Prep](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/tutorials/meeting-prep/meeting-prep.md): Build a meeting prep agent using Linkup inside Xpander
- [Frequently Asked Questions](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/faq/faq.md)
- [Typescript SDK](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/sdk/js/js.md): How to use Linkup Javascript SDK natively in your apps.
- [Python SDK](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/sdk/python/python.md): How to use Linkup Python SDK natively in your apps.
- [OpenAI SDK](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/sdk/open-ai/open-ai.md): How to use OpenAI SDK natively in your apps.
- [CLI](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/sdk/cli/cli.md): How to use the Linkup CLI from your terminal and scripts.
- [/search](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/search/reference.md): The `/search` endpoint allows you to retrieve web content.
- [/fetch](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/fetch/reference.md): The `/fetch` endpoint allows you to fetch a single webpage from a given URL.
- [/research](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/research/post.md): The `POST /research` method creates an asynchronous research task which can perform a comprehensive web research.
- [/research](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/research/list.md): The `GET /research` method, without research task identifier, lists all created research tasks for the authenticated organization, with pagination.
- [/research/:id](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/research/get.md): The `GET /research/:id` method, with research task identifier, retrieves a specific research task information.
- [/tasks](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/tasks/post.md): The `/tasks` endpoint allows you to run Linkup's `/search`, `/fetch`, and `/research` calls in batch and asynchronously.
- [/tasks](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/tasks/list.md): The `GET /tasks` method, without a task identifier, lists all created tasks for the authenticated organization, with pagination.
- [/tasks/:id](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/tasks/get.md): The `GET /tasks/:id` method, with task identifier, retrieves a specific task information.
- [/extract](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/extract/post.md): [BETA] The `POST /extract` method creates an asynchronous extract task.
- [/extract](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/extract/list.md): [BETA] The `GET /extract` method, without extract task identifier, lists all created extract tasks for the authenticated organization, with pagination.
- [/extract/:id](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/extract/get.md): [BETA] The `GET /extract/:id` method, with extract task identifier, retrieves a specific extract task information.
- [/credits/balance](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/documentation/endpoints/account/balance.md): The `/credits/balance` endpoint allows you to retrieve your current credits balance.
- [Integrations](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/integrations.md): How to integrate Linkup in your application.
- [Linkup MCP Server](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/mcp/mcp.md): Linkup MCP Server allows you to use the Linkup API in your MCP clients.
- [Linkup Skills](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/linkup-skill.md): Reusable knowledge modules that teach AI agents how to use Linkup effectively
- [Linkup + OpenClaw](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/openclaw/openclaw.md): Integrate Linkup with OpenClaw to give your self-hosted agent real-time web search via the clawhub skill registry
- [Vercel AI SDK](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/vercel-ai-sdk.md): How to use Linkup with the Vercel AI SDK
- [Langchain](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/langchain.md): How to use Linkup with our Langchain SDK
- [CrewAI](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/crewai.md): Use Linkup as a web search tool with CrewAI multi-agent systems
- [LlamaIndex](https://docs.linkup.so/pages/integrations/llama-index.md): How to use Linkup in LlamaIndex
